WEBVTT

00:00:01.078 --> 00:00:09.737
A whole visit, start to end. In Session, type the patient ID and press Next: the session starts in the chosen BIDS folder.

00:00:15.162 --> 00:00:23.205
Choose the DBS indication, here OCD, the anatomical target, the lead model and the IPG.

00:00:40.895 --> 00:00:47.626
The initial assessment documents how the patient arrives: the clinical scales, the medications and a note.

00:01:05.944 --> 00:01:17.319
Then the stimulation on arrival: 130 hertz, 5 milliamps, 90 microseconds on each side. Tap a contact twice for a cathode, and the case once for the anode.

00:01:28.195 --> 00:01:36.819
In Programming, raise the amplitude to 6 milliamps, rate the symptoms and side effects, note how the patient responds, and save.

00:01:56.878 --> 00:02:03.876
At 7 milliamps the patient is better: the configuration is starred and marked as the final settings.

00:02:28.011 --> 00:02:31.016
At 8 milliamps, side effects appear.

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:57.318
The charts follow every rating across the configurations, and the table lists them all.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:06.888
Next confirms the configuration the patient leaves on. Finish makes the reports and the BIDS export.

